-- Q9: hospitalized due to my son biting me in the ankle; proof of the
-- wellness visit was provided 6 months after the effective date; I was
-- serving as a police officer at the time of hospitalization. Stated:
-- the CAUSE of the injury is a domestic incident (a bite), not police
-- duty — "serving as a police officer at the time" is a status/
-- occupation fact, not a causal one, so `causes` is left empty (the
-- Section 2.1(4) exclusion requires the injury to have arisen out of
-- police service, not merely that the claimant happens to be a police
-- officer). Ground `Accidental injury`; `written confirmation month`
-- JUST 6 (within the 7-month deadline).
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                  IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`             IS 6
    `hospitalization ground`            IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`            IS 30
    `causes`                            IS EMPTY
    `fraud month`                       IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`           IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`              IS JUST 3
    `wellness visit provider qualified` IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`        IS JUST 6
    `dispute arisen`                    IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`            IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`       IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`    IS FALSE
    `written proof of claim month`      IS NOTHING
    `recovery sought month`             IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                IS 12

